WEBVTT

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.290
We will now begin our meeting to
discuss the investigation into the series of

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.540
robberies targeting the wealthy that
occurred in the Yokohama Division today.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.580
The suspect has committed four robberies
in the short span of three hours

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.910
and is currently at large.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.660
Proceed with the investigation using
footage of the suspect that was obtained

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.620
from a security camera in
the vicinity as your primary reference.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.290
Based on subsequent footage
from this security camera,

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.040
the suspect is believed to have
been headed toward the Minami area.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.120
Find whatever clues you can
to locate him. Dismissed.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.790
"Yokohama Police Station"

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.410
Samatoki?

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.040
What do you want at this hour?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.330
"Indomitable"

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.620
It's not like you to be callin' me up.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.950
"Indomitable"

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.950
You got some business with me?

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.870
Yeah, I need your guys' help.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.040
Sure thing. I'm all ears.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.000
Yeah, Tom, that's right.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.450
Things have become a real mess
at Jyuto Iruma's day job.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.160
If this keeps up, his team's
chances at the qualifiers are at risk.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.910
I'll call you back later.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.790
Sorry, guys.
We've got orders from above to haul in

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.450
any and every suspicious
character roaming 'Hama's streets.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.790
W-We were just on our way to
have some d-drinks with our friends--

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:41.660
First, let's see some ID.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.790
This doesn't look like you.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.500
N-No way...

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.620
This one doesn't match either.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.000
These look suspicious.
We'll have to confiscate them.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.830
Hey, what the fuck's your problem?

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.950
--Go! Now!
--Y-Yes, ma'am...

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.950
May we have a moment of your time?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.200
We'd like to ask you a few questions.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.540
You, too. Show me your badge.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.040
Tsk.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.620
That's a sweet ride you've got there.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.120
It wouldn't happen to be
illegally modified, now would it?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.330
She might have something to hide.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.750
All right, I'll talk...

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.950
...with your superiors while we
comfortably enjoy a special screening of <i>this</i>.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.870
The bitch got it all on camera!

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:47.250
Keep your filthy paws off me.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.290
I might accidentally hit the "send all" button.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.160
Grrr.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.580
C'mon, let's go.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.080
Tsk.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.870
What an obnoxious bitch!

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.000
Forget about her.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.040
You'll feel a helluva lot better once
you see the pathetic look on Iruma's face.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.830
Heh, you've got that right.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:10.080
Iruma? Jyuto Iruma?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.330
No luck, huh?

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.450
I came back empty-handed, too.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.250
The qualifiers start at 10 AM.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.870
It doesn't look like I can make it in time.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.540
The tournament rules state that
there must be three people per team.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.120
If you started looking right now
for someone to replace me, you just might...

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.250
Samatoki, I'm sorry, but--

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.410
Don't gimme that bullshit!
What the fuck are you sorry for, bastard?

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.870
The score I've gotta settle with Ichiro?
Its connection with Chuohku?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.910
You tellin' me you're sorry for crushin' my
motivation to win the division battle?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.040
The <i>three of us </i>are MAD TRIGGER CREW!
You got that?

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:59.370
We'll show the world that we're
invincible beyond a shadow of a doubt.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.160
I also believe it would be best for us
to fight using our present resources.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.410
Replacing personnel is out of the question.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.790
You're right.
There's nothing we can't do. Right?

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:13.000
So, don't hang up your gloves.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.080
We still got time, you know.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.040
You guys are really tight!

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:22.620
But you guys should know that there
are lowlifes out there who are jealous of you.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.330
Who the hell are you?

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.200
It doesn't matter who I am.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.910
What <i>does </i>matter is what I've got to show you.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.700
Those guys mentioned you by name, Jyuto Iruma.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.200
I wasn't at all interested in the slimebags,

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.790
but still, I had one of
my hacker friends look into them.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.200
One of your hacker friends?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.330
Yeah, the guy claims to be a
video game creator from Dubai or something.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:21.790
It's looking like MAD TRIGGER CREW's
gonna advance to the finals, Big Bro.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.450
Samatoki, huh?

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:26.790
I've gotta make sure that
<i>I'm </i>the one to finish him off.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.580
Saburo, what's taking you so long?
Hurry up and finish that!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.370
Big Bro's waiting, you know!!

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.080
Sorry, Brother Ichi.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.040
One of my hacker friends
asked me to do something for him...

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.910
He wants me to use facial recognition

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.450
to find somebody out of a group of SNS images.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:42.700
For cryin' out loud,

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.700
what would some ramen
shop owner in his fifties use this for?

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.950
Wow, this hacker runs a ramen shop?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.950
I'm pretty sure it's totally made-up.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.450
For one thing, I'm passing myself off
as a video game creator from Dubai.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.870
So, I found out that those two
are some pretty tough customers.

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:08.080
The lowest of the low, so to speak.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.410
Sounds like you've got
something against the police.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.200
Oh, really? How could you tell?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:16.540
Since I was a kid, I've had more
than my share of run-ins with the cops.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.870
A cop who's chummy with the yakuza
has gotta be a major scumbag.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.080
I couldn't say.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:27.580
But I guess there might be a few
decent apples among all the cops out there.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.040
One would only hope so.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.500
I suppose the same
can be said of any organization.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.950
Hmph. You got that right.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.540
Wh-What are you doing?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.790
What does it look like?

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:01.450
We're arresting a serial robber, of course.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.660
What do you mean "arresting"?

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:04.410
Hey, that wasn't part of the plan.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.660
You said the stolen money'd be split equally.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.660
Yeah, and that's what we're going to do.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:12.040
But we can't split it equally three ways.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:17.540
So, he and I will split it evenly between
the two of us and savor it ourselves.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.200
N-No way...

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.580
End of discussion!

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.120
No! Don't!

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.160
H-Help...

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.540
I-It hurts...

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.500
Case closed.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:37.620
"And we all lived happily ever after."

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.250
Wh-Who the hell are you?

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.540
I-Iruma?!

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.330
Kudos to my esteemed elders!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:56.000
I'm amazed you collared the perp.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:01.000
Who would've thought you were
hiding him in a police safe house?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.410
And to think that you'd try to divvy up
the stolen goods between the two of you...

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.540
You guys really <i>are </i>the lowest of the low.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.450
Which is worse, a cop in bed with
the yakuza or the ones in bed with a perp?

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.540
Why don't you tell me, <i>huh</i>?!

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.040
Looks like we'll just have
to kick all your asses at once!

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.870
And we'll be doin' some ass kickin' of our own.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.040
♬ You three, enough of your
inane activities, I must interject ♬

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:45.410
♬ I'm a space cowboy, orbiting the suspect ♬

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.750
♬ I don't need no warrant to make a sting ♬

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.290
♬ Disappearing evidence is no big thing (shh) ♬

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.540
♬ 45 Rabbit the rules don't apply to me ♬

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.080
♬ You better not mess with MTC (right?) ♬

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.410
♬ I have on my side yakuza and ex-military ♬

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:00.500
♬ Thanks for doing all
the hard work for me (yes sir) ♬

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.040
♬ Codename Crazy M ♬

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.160
♬ One minute after deployment
there's nothing left of them (yes sir) ♬

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.000
♬ Target eliminated ♬

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.660
♬ To breakthrough is to have
the field of intel gathering dominated ♬

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.580
♬ A deserter who violated regulation ♬

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:14.370
♬ Time is at hand for your execution ♬

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.540
♬ Mission accomplished, surprise attack went great ♬

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:19.080
♬ 2 DIE 4, I do not hesitate ♬

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.250
♬ The first lesson is "sit" when training a puppy ♬

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.830
♬ I'll beat into you the laws of this hierarchy ♬

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:26.080
♬ "Show me liars and I'll show you thieves" ♬

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.620
♬ Mr. Officer, don't you agree?
(fuck the police) ♬

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.040
♬ If it were up to my underlings
you'd be missing a head ♬

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.500
♬ Your plot doesn't connect the dots ♬

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.160
♬ How you go belly up don't matter ♬

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:38.790
♬ I call the shots
(Mr.hard core) ♬

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.450
♬ Hey! Do or nothing ♬

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:43.040
♬ My words are the bullets and
I'm locked and loaded, hell yeah ♬

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.450
♬ Bang Bang
We're Mad Trigger, you know? ♬

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.830
♬ Make us your enemy and it's over ♬

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.450
♬ Bad Warrior ♬

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.120
♬ Hey! Do or nothing ♬

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.660
♬ Bullets buried in your brain, hell yeah ♬

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.000
♬ Bang Bang
Yeah, you better brace for disgrace ♬

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.370
♬ Taking out the trash around town ♬

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.040
♬ Hama's cleaning crew ♬

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:12.250
♬ HEY HEY HEY HEY HEY HEY HEY HEY ♬

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.830
I'll be gracious and overlook what you've done.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.790
Huh?! S-So, you'll let us go?

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.790
Eh heh heh heh...

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:25.290
You are now my slaves for as long as you live.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:30.500
You'll be working your fingers to
the bone in order to advance my career.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.290
Keh heh heh heh heh heh...

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.950
Sgt. Iruma, wait!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.700
Today aren't you and I...

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.620
Congratulations! You're ready
to stand on your own two feet.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:59.660
Huh?! Sgt. Iruma...

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:02.040
What about the investigation?

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.620
It's already been closed.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.540
And the winner is... MAD TRIGGER CREW!!

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.330
Unghhh...

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.750
All right...

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.080
...already...

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.040
I'm coming, I'm coming...

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.910
Hello?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.910
H-Hold up.

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:40.290
I'm not following what you're saying.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.160
What about Dice?

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:44.580
He lost at gambling <i>again</i>?

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:48.120
I'm fed up with hearing about that. Bye, now.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.450
But are you sure it's all right?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.620
Looks like your team's all gone off
to do their own thing...

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.370
I see.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:07.580
So, on top of being saddled
with 10 million yen in gambling debts,

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.580
Dice is being held captive?

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.700
Yep. In the underground casino
of that building over there, you see.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.410
It's only a three-minute walk.
Can you believe it?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.410
Shibuya Division's so small!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:20.250
So, why are you tagging along, Gentaro?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.540
I am at an impasse in my writing.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.540
Why art thou going, Ramuda?

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.330
I had trouble sleeping in today. Ah-hahahaha.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:30.540
By the way, the division battle
qualifiers are tomorrow.

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:33.120
--Of course, you'll be there, right?
--I shan't be going.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.910
Well, that was but a lie.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.410
So, does that mean you <i>are </i>coming?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:38.160
That, too, was but a lie.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.200
Eh-hehe...

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.200
If we're gonna make it to the finals,

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:45.450
we've gotta start coming together
a bit more as a team.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.450
"Free Mahjong 2F"
"Ramen"

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.250
Ungh! Let go of me!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.250
Pardon the intrusion!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.580
Ramuda! Gentaro!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.540
Hey, there! Thanks for your trouble!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.750
Who's the kind human who called me up?

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:12.540
Oh well, I guess it doesn't matter much.
Thanks for taking such good care of Dice.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.750
Hold up there.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.370
Whatcha gonna do about the 10 mil
that this punk blew while he was here?

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:21.580
The money he owes us
following his gambling spree.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:22.950
They must've cheated!

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.790
Ain't no way I could lose like that!

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.580
Hmm. This is starting to sound
like a real pain in the neck,

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.040
so why don't I just fork over the 10 mil?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.450
Ramuda!

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:35.080
Um, actually, I changed my mind.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.120
Let's do this a different way.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.330
Huh? What do you mean by "a different way"?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:46.790
I kinda get the feeling that it was
karma that brought all three of you here.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:48.870
Oh, gee! You think?

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.870
So, it was our destiny, right?

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:53.540
We're gonna play a game,
and you're gonna bet your voices on it.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.000
What?! Our voices?!

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.290
Hmm...

00:15:56.290 --> 00:16:01.290
We had a real terrible time
once 'cause of you, Fling Posse.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.580
What are you talking about?

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:09.290
Once at one of your freestyle battles,
we bet on the other team.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.200
As if that weren't enough,

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:16.370
you guys clobbered 'em,
and we lost some serious dough...

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.120
Betting on battles...

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.120
That's a big no-no!

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:24.870
So, all I'm sayin' is we should settle his
gambling debts with a friendly wager.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:28.410
If you guys win, we'll forget
about what he owes us.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:33.700
But if we win, Fling Posse,
we get to wreck all of your voices.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.040
Huh.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.750
But how?

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.080
Oh, it's easy.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.500
We'll just stick a blow-dryer in
your mouths and turn it on full blast.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.750
All we're gonna do is burn
your vocal cords and ruin them.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.540
It's not like you'll die or anything.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:48.330
But you can call it a <i>wrap</i>
to your lives as <i>rappers</i>.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.580
Ah-hahahaha!

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:54.830
The voices of the three of us, huh?

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.160
--Okay!
--What are you sayin', you moron?!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.750
Ramuda! Gentaro! Run for your lives!

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:01.330
What are you gonna do, Gentaro?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.080
Methinks 'twould not be so bad to investigate

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.500
the heart-pounding thrill of gambling
that Dice always speaketh of.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.870
Guys...

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.410
Okay, so what are we gonna play?

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:13.580
I don't wanna play anything too hard, you know?

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:16.950
Don't worry, it's just a simple dice game.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:18.290
You roll two dice,

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.910
and the person who rolls
the highest number of pips wins.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.950
When you say "the number of pips,"

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.200
you mean the number of pips facing up, right?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.250
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.000
All righty then,
let's get this over with in a jiffy!

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.200
This ain't somethin' we should do in a jiffy!

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.660
C'mon now! Let me roll the dice!

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.120
You said it yourself.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:38.040
"We should settle his gambling
debts with a friendly wager."

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:40.000
So, you can't let some amateur do it!

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.500
This has gotta be a contest
between two gamblers!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.870
Oh, all right.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.540
Oh! Sorry you guys had
to come on account of me...

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.250
Don't misconstrue mine intentions.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.450
I'm here for mine own reasons.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.200
C'mon, Dice! Let me be the one to do it!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.250
This here...

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.370
...is a job for <i>me</i>!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.410
You okay with us goin' first?

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.250
Sure.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.750
All right. Let's begin.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.200
Using my ever-trusty trick dice.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:13.750
This pair is weighed so they always roll sixes.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.870
Yes!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:26.290
Well, lookie here!
Rolled boxcars right from the start!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:36.450
If he hath a score of twelve,
our chances of winning are naught.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:38.870
--That's for sure.
--'Tis a draw at best.

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:43.620
Still, the probability of that is 1 in 36.

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.830
Nope. The probability is zero.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.540
Those dice always roll ones.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:51.410
It's plain to see you're gonna lose!

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:56.200
But Dice is a trusted member of my posse, so...

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.120
there's no way that things'll end here.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.120
Dost thou speak in earnest?

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.660
"'Twas but a lie."

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.450
Just kidding!

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.870
Uwoahhhhhh!

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:21.250
Here goes nothin'!

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:27.830
Heh!

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.660
The left die is a one.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:33.910
The right die standeth on edge,
and three of its faces point upwards.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.120
What the--?!

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:40.580
Yes! 1 + 2 + 4 + 6 for a total of 13!

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:42.200
Well, well!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.660
Holy cow! We won, Dice!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.910
Don't mess with us!

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.330
You call that a roll?!

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.540
Oh, really? Ramuda double
checked with you, didn't he?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.500
That "the number of pips
facing up" count as the roll.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.160
You cheated!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.580
Cheated?!

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:57.950
What a load of crap!

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:01.910
These are the dice I got from <i>you</i>! Huh?

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.500
Come now, Dice.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.620
Quickly, now. Bite into it.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.500
Huh?

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.830
What the--?!

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.000
<i>You guys </i>were the ones that cheated!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.830
Damn... Now that the secret's out,
it looks like we got no other choice!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:19.370
Oh, so now you're gonna
take us on in a rap battle?

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.370
--What are we gonna do, guys?
--This should prove amusing.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.200
Let's kick some ass!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.870
The three of us...
Fling Posse'll take you all on!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.160
All righty then, here we go!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:35.450
♬ Hey, hey, hey, no cheating! ♬

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:38.040
♬ I simply despise lies ♬

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:40.250
♬ How dare you trick me.... ♬

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.580
♬ Not enough skill, not enough thrill ♬

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:46.450
♬ Begone fake, the answer is real ♬

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:49.120
♬ Before your eyes,
giving the goddess of victory a kiss ♬

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.500
--♬ Strike a ♬
--♬ Rhythm ♬

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:51.910
♬ Rhymes are my chips ♬

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.580
♬ Already boiling ♬

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:57.330
♬ Double or nothing, roll the dice of destiny ♬

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.000
♬ Snake eyes of course, naturally ♬

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.370
♬ Fling Posse, all OK, win this GAME ♬

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:06.080
♬ JACKPOT JACKPOT ♬

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.290
♬ Three people here are HOT SHOTS ♬

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.910
♬ No business with anyone wack, so holla ♬

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:14.290
♬ I'll end this, Game over ♬

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.750
♬ JACKPOT JACKPOT ♬

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.410
♬ Three people here are HOT SHOTS ♬

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.830
♬ No business with anyone wack, so holla ♬

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:24.620
♬ I'll end this, Game over ♬

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:31.450
"24 Udagawacho"

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:39.200
Heh...

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.120
Looks like they've come together as a team.

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.790
Ah-hahahahahahaha!

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.410
Ah!

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.410
And the winner is... Fling Posse!

